>> How to Create LVM Partition in Linux
   Link : https://www.learnitguide.net/2016/06/how-to-create-lvm-partition-in-linux.html

1. Identify the volume we want to convert it into logical volume. 
2.  Create Physical Volumes (PV) on the disk.
   command: pvcreate /dev/xvdf
   Note : It can be more than one volume . 
   ## Command to check Physical volume
    pvscan
    pvdisplay pvname   
3. Create Volume Group (VG) on the Physical Volumes
    command : vgcreate datavg /dev/sdf   
      here datavg --> volume group name , /dev/sdf --> physical volume name 

    ## Command to check logical volume 
    vgdisplay -v datavg 
    here: datavg ---> logical group name 
4. Create Logical Volumes (LV) on the Volume Group
    command: lvcreate -L 99G -n datavol1 datavg 

    here : 99G --> size of volume,  datavol1 --> logical volume name ,datavg--> volume group name 

5. Create filesystem for the logical volumes.
    command: mkfs.ext4 /dev/datavg/datavol1 

6. To mount the volume 
    command : mount /dev/datavg/datavol1 /data 


